# The commands of msil/utils/msil-prog.py (plan 5.12.4), from what it prints
# when %msil_prog_build runs with the stand-ins of lit.local.cfg:
# (1) MSIL mode (lto, il): each source compiled for the MSIL triple with
#     %{msil_cflags}, -<L>, -flto and -c from the build directory, under a
#     path relative to it; a stock source for the native triple with -flto
#     (-fno-ms-volatile on windows-msvc only); each archive member into
#     ar/<NAME>/ and 'rcs ar/<NAME>/lib<NAME>.a' in member order; the link
#     through the clang driver with --ld-path=<msil-ld>, -<L>,
#     %{msil_ldflags} (from M15 no -nodefaultlibs: empty on a Windows triple,
#     --sysroot=<msil_linux_sysroot> on a Linux triple), the objects, the
#     stock objects, -Lar/<NAME> -l<NAME>, the --lib arguments in order, the
#     --native-lib arguments (%{msil_native_libs}), -Wl,--lto-emit-asm and
#     -o prog.il; then ilasm -exe of prog.il into --out, and --also-il copies
#     prog.il;
# (2) native mode through the driver for a Linux triple: ordinary compiles
#     for the native triple (no -flto, also for stock sources and members),
#     archives lib<NAME>.a, and -fuse-ld=lld with the --native-lib arguments
#     and then %{msil_native_ldflags} at the end and no MSIL link argument;
# (3) the same for windows-msvc, where the archive is <NAME>.lib (the MSVC
#     driver turns -l<NAME> into <NAME>.lib); a Windows host only, because
#     the stand-in's Windows program is a .NET Framework executable;
# (4) native mode with the E7 Linux oracle (plan 5.12.8): compiles for
#     x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu with -fno-pic, start.c compiled as the E7
#     oracle compiles it, and ld.lld -dynamic-linker
#     /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --as-needed -rpath $ORIGIN start.o
#     <objects> <archives> <the --native-lib arguments, -Wl,A,B written as
#     A B> followed by the sysroot's libm.so.6, libc.so.6 and libgcc_s.so.1
#     (-rpath $ORIGIN: a test-built shared library that msil-run.py --dep
#     copies next to the program is found there; M15).
# The later --triple, --native-ldflags, --ld-lld, --linux-sysroot and
# --start options win over those of %msil_prog_build, which names the E7
# oracle under the WSL runner; empty ones cancel them for (2) and (3).

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/sysroot/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu
# RUN: %{harness_check} write %t/sysroot/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so.6
# RUN: %{harness_check} write %t/sysroot/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6
# RUN: %{harness_check} write %t/sysroot/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libgcc_s.so.1

